  "title": "Ex 2.6 #10 · (P ⇒ Q) ∨ R vs ∼((P ∧ ∼Q) ∧ ∼R)",
  "prompt": "Are $(P \\Rightarrow Q) \\vee R$ and $\\sim ((P \\wedge \\sim Q) \\wedge \\sim R)$ logically equivalent? Decide, and back up your answer with a truth table, a chain of known equivalences, or a row where the two statements differ.",
  "answer_format": "equivalent or not equivalent. Steps are optional: truth-table columns, rewrite steps, or a row like P = T, Q = F where the two statements differ.",
